1	/**
2	 * @file
3	 * @copyright SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
4	 *
5	 * @test @b mrn_rmw_diff_64k
6	 * @test @b mrn_rmw_diff_1m
7	 * @parblock
8	 * Footprint scan probe for core-179 SDC — isolates whether the L1D-array
9	 * read path still triggers when the buffer reaches / exceeds L1D capacity.
10	 *
11	 * Context (see memory footprint-independent-of-l1d-size &
12	 * sdc-rootcause-is-hardware-not-timing): three SDC-triggering tests span
13	 * footprint 64B (mrn_rmw_fwd, ~1 cache line) .. 16KB (mrn_rmw_diff, 0.25x
14	 * L1D) .. 128KB (movbe_dump, 2x L1D). All trigger. This already shows
15	 * footprint SIZE is not the trigger. The open question this probe answers:
16	 *
17	 *   Does the L1D-array read path (different-address str->ldr, NOT forwarding)
18	 *   still trigger when the buffer is EXACTLY L1D-sized (4-way thrash edge)
19	 *   vs when it far exceeds L1D (every reload misses L1D, served from L2)?
20	 *
21	 * Both tests reuse mrn_rmw_diff's different-address design: str res->tempA[i],
22	 * then ldr from tempB[i] (DIFFERENT address). tempB is pre-filled with the
23	 * golden value. The reload CANNOT be served by store-buffer forwarding (the
24	 * str wrote tempA, not tempB), so it must come from the cache array. The
25	 * only variable across these two tests is the tempB buffer size (= how
26	 * much of L1D the reload stream touches).
27	 *
28	 *   - mrn_rmw_diff_64k: tempB = 64KB == L1D (64KB/4-way/64B). 1024 lines map
29	 *     to 256 sets x 4 ways -> each set gets exactly 4 lines -> the stream
30	 *     JUST fills L1D, sitting on the thrash edge. Reload is L1D-array read
31	 *     under capacity pressure.  If trigger rate ~= mrn_rmw_diff(16KB),
32	 *     capacity/thrash is NOT an amplifier.  If rate spikes, it IS.
33	 *   - mrn_rmw_diff_1m:  tempB = 1MB = 16x L1D.  Every tempB[i] reload misses
34	 *     L1D (no way the line is resident after a 1MB sweep), served from
35	 *     L2/L3 refill -> load port.  Data leaves L1D entirely.  If SDC
36	 *     disappears here (0 fail) while _64k triggers, the defect needs the
37	 *     load to HIT L1D array (path mechanism), not merely str->ldr timing
38	 *     (which is unchanged).  If SDC persists, it favors pure-timing.
39	 *
40	 * Hot loop byte-identical to mrn_rmw_diff (same str/ldr/ALU, same indices),
41	 * only MRN_RMW_DIFF_COUNT differs.  Miscompare logging in cold branch only
42	 * (see memory dump-variant-noremove-report-fail-verified: touching even the
43	 * cold branch once silenced the defect; we keep report_fail_msg as-is).
44	 * @endparblock
